#+TITLE: Global page heap exposes an AutoCAD startup wide-string over-read
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: vendor-cad-validation

* Evidence
An isolated pure-COM AutoCAD2022 instance under the existing EPURE account
and selected Epure profile, with full page heap, faults before quiescence.
PID33364, first-chance full dump3767186581 bytes, SHA256
7f8f0cdf97d5d7f210debc2ff078f56d30a264e4d2e6a77543dc3a8337fa8a51.
No ALFE/Lisp test or Quit request was involved.
VCRUNTIME140+10B36 is memcpy_avx_ermsb_amd+126, a16-byte load crossing a
protected page. The source is8 bytes into an allocated14-byte buffer.
The matching allocated DPH stamp and direct ExceptionStream are captured.
PE unwind tables show accore wide-string helpers requesting8 wchar_t from
that short source, followed by accore/acad/MFC initialization frames.
No proprietary EPURE native code appears in that stack; the profile/input
trigger and exact internal Autodesk function names remain unclassified.
This is not proof of the original MFC thread-state shutdown corruption.

* Operational result
Quiescence timed out, then the exact owned CAD required forced cleanup.
Do not qualify shutdown from this run. The administrator controller restored
the image option, removed its task and released both runners. No binary or
product source was patched. All dump/binary analysis was performed off Windows.

* Next evidence
Preserve this as a separate startup over-read. Narrow full guard pages to
480-byte allocations to investigate the original thread-state lifetime bug;
verify the effective filter in that next capture. Obtain matching Autodesk
symbols/source if needed to name the startup helper and its input contract.
Detailed evidence is in
[[file:../../autolisp-front-end/documentation/epure-autocad-shutdown-offline-analysis.org]].
